and at once she knew him, indeed, bustling about
the man-glorifying battle, her own brother
and her husband’s brother, and she rejoiced in her heart;

And she set out to go to the chamber, which for her her dear son made,
Hephaestus, and close-fitting doors to the doorposts he fitted
with a hidden bolt, which no other god opened;

With ambrosia first from her skin, full of longing,
all the filth she cleansed away, and she anointed herself richly with oil,
ambrosial, sweet, which for her had been perfumed;

and she girded herself with a girdle, fitted with a hundred tassels,
and in the well-pierced lobes she put earrings,
three-eyed, mulberry-like;

